WTFOOD — Account & Data Deletion

This page explains how to delete your WTFOOD account and data, for anyone who wants to do this from within the app or without it.

Option 1: Delete your account from within the app
Open WTFOOD and sign in.
Go to Preferences.
Tap Delete my account.
Confirm the deletion when prompted.

This takes effect immediately.

Option 2: Request deletion without using the app

If you no longer have access to the app, or can't sign in (for example, you've lost access to the email or Google account tied to your WTFOOD account), email pauldzamara@gmail.com with the subject line "Account deletion request" from the email address associated with your account, or including whatever details you can provide to help us identify the account. We'll confirm your identity as best we can and process the request manually.

Requests are normally completed within a few days, and no later than 30 days.

What gets deleted

When your account is deleted, we immediately:

Revoke all active sessions, so the account can no longer be signed into.
Anonymize your email address, name, and profile picture, so the account can no longer identify you personally.
Delete or mark as deleted: your allergy and dietary preferences, saved dietary profiles, scan history, saved product lists, and community product submissions tied to your account.

None of this data is recoverable once deletion is confirmed.

What isn't affected
Product and ingredient data you contributed (e.g. a barcode you helped add to our database) may remain in the shared product database in de-identified form — it's about the product, not about you, and isn't reversed by account deletion.
Standard technical server logs (e.g. IP addresses kept briefly for security/abuse-prevention purposes) follow our normal short retention period regardless of account status; they are not linked to your deleted account.
Deleting only some of your data, without deleting your whole account

You don't have to delete your entire account to remove specific things:

Allergy and dietary preferences — clear these any time from the Preferences screen. Takes effect immediately.
Saved dietary profiles — delete individual profiles from the Preferences screen.
Saved product lists — delete a list, or individual items within it, at any time.

Scan history is currently only removable as part of full account deletion — there isn't yet a way to clear just your history while keeping the rest of your account. If you want this changed before deleting anything else, contact us and we'll do it manually in the meantime.

